course: dictionary
lesson: 11551
title: Amplification: louder or more detail
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Amplification is a long word, but it is linked to the verb amplify, which means to make bigger or stronger. It has two main meanings. The first is about sound or signals: making them louder or stronger. «The speaker's amplification made the music fill the whole park.»
explain: The second meaning is more formal. When someone adds detail to explain a point better, that is amplification. «The teacher gave more amplification of her idea, with two real examples.» The idea stays the same, but it is explained more fully.
explain: Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. Words such as speaker, music or volume point to the first meaning. Words such as idea, point or explain point to the second. Swap in "making louder" or "adding detail" and see which still makes sense.
fact: Amplification means making a sound or signal louder or stronger.
fact: In a formal sense, amplification means adding more detail to explain something better.
fact: Amplification is a noun, and its plural is amplifications.
fact: You will often meet it in science lessons about sound and electricity, where speakers and amplifiers give amplification.
fact: Useful phrases: «sound amplification» and «needs amplification».
exercise: «The speaker gave the singer's voice amplification, so the whole park could hear.» What does amplification mean here? | Turning the lights off | Stopping the music | Making the singer sing slower | *Making the sound louder
exercise: «Her answer needed more amplification, so she added two examples.» What does amplification mean here? | Making the answer shorter | Forgetting the answer | Making the sound quieter | *Adding more detail to explain better
exercise: Which word is the plural of amplification? | amplifyings | amplificates | *amplifications | amplifiers
test: «The microphone and amplifier gave the sound amplification.» What does this sound become? | Shorter | Slower | Quieter | *Louder
test: «Mum asked for more amplification of the plan, so I explained each step.» What does amplification mean here? | Making the plan shorter | Throwing the plan away | *Adding more detail | Making the plan louder
exam: Which sentence uses amplification in the formal sense of adding detail? | «The amplifier gave the guitar more amplification.» | «The amplification of the lights was very bright.» | «The crowd heard amplification from the stage.» | *«The author gave more amplification of her argument, with facts and examples.»
